license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/mertgulerx/world-collection"
url: "https://github.com/mertgulerx/world-collection"

abstract: >-
  World Collection is a set of 42 Gazebo Harmonic worlds for testing
  autonomous exploration, navigation and SLAM in simulation. The worlds
  are grouped by purpose: ten single-challenge worlds, each built around
  one layout feature such as a narrow passage, dead ends, a loop, clutter
  or open space; two pilot worlds for setup and parameter tuning;
  twenty-five worlds from five seeded generated families (mazes, offices,
  warehouse aisles, forests and city blocks) that vary size, rooms,
  doors or density in a controlled way; three worlds based on real
  places; and two worlds with moving obstacles whose motion depends only
  on simulation time. Every world is a plain SDF file without a robot and
  comes with fixed start poses and measured layout values, including
  free area, narrowest passage, loops, dead ends and visibility
  descriptors. The worlds are generated by an included Python package
  that checks each world and rebuilds it to identical files.

keywords:
  - Gazebo
  - simulation worlds
  - autonomous exploration
  - robot navigation
  - SLAM
  - benchmarking
  - mobile robotics
  - procedural generation
  - moving obstacles
  - ROS 2
